       "text": "I won't enter ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily (6400 mg/day). It's twice the labeled maximum daily dose. I'm not aware of any indication that calls for it, and the harm could be serious: GI hemorrhage, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. Documenting your decision in the chart doesn't lower that risk for the patient.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- Ibuprofen 800 mg by mouth four times daily (3200 mg/day, the maximum).\n- Ibuprofen 600 mg by mouth four times daily (2400 mg/day).\n- Ibuprofen at a lower dose, combined with scheduled acetaminophen or another adjunct if you need more analgesia.\n\nIf you have a specialized protocol in mind, such as high-dose ibuprofen with level monitoring, tell me the indication and details. If you still want the dose as written, a pharmacist review or a direct order through your hospital's override process would be the appropriate route, not me."
